Reduce per-frame Image allocation for the circle approach ring.

Circle.draw() ran getScaledCopy(approachScale) once per visible circle per
frame, allocating a throwaway Image each time. Image.draw(x, y, w, h, color)
renders at an arbitrary size using the same TextureRegion with no allocation.

Note the original `if` had no braces, so the replacement must add them.

--- a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/objects/Circle.java
+++ b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/objects/Circle.java
@@ -113,7 +113,11 @@
 		float oldAlpha = Colors.WHITE_FADE.a;
 		Colors.WHITE_FADE.a = color.a = alpha;
 
-		if (timeDiff >= 0 && !GameMod.HIDDEN.isActive())
-			GameImage.APPROACHCIRCLE.getImage().getScaledCopy(approachScale).drawCentered(x, y, color);
+		if (timeDiff >= 0 && !GameMod.HIDDEN.isActive()) {
+			Image approachCircle = GameImage.APPROACHCIRCLE.getImage();
+			float acWidth = approachCircle.getWidth() * approachScale;
+			float acHeight = approachCircle.getHeight() * approachScale;
+			approachCircle.draw(x - acWidth / 2f, y - acHeight / 2f, acWidth, acHeight, color);
+		}
 		GameImage.HITCIRCLE.getImage().drawCentered(x, y, color);
 		boolean overlayAboveNumber = Options.getSkin().isHitCircleOverlayAboveNumber();
